  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "The proposal investigates the impact of gamification (points/levels) on engagement and learning outcomes in LLM-PATs. It employs a mixed-methods approach (quantitative study + qualitative interviews) to address three sub-RQs, focusing on engagement dimensions, learning outcomes, and user characteristics. The theoretical framework on gamification for learning and controlled experimental design are central to the methodology.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Strengths",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#404040",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "With a clear learning goal, this proposal aims to understand how gamification influences engagement and learning outcomes in the context of LLM-PATs for Higher Education. Several concrete sub-research questions have been proposed for exploration.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The literature review for existing studies is extensive.",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The methodology part is clear and well-defined grounded on a theoretical framework, which provides a robust foundation for the proposal",
    "attributes": {
      "color": "#000000",
      "background": "transparent"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": ".",
    "attributes": {
